menu "Michi Music Stream Audio Engine"

    comment "RTP/UDP session engine (phase 11): PCM S16LE 48 kHz stereo, packet jitter buffer, metrics. Future metas (S24LE, 44.1-96 kHz, RTCP, drift, source auth, multiroom) are declared in michi_audio.h, not implemented."

    config MICHI_AUDIO_RTP_PT_S16LE
        int "RTP payload type for PCM S16LE"
        default 10
        range 0 127
        help
          RTP payload type (PT) the session accepts as PCM S16LE.
          The default 10 reuses the RFC 3551 L16 slot, but with the
          project's LITTLE-endian convention: a compliant RFC 3551
          L16 sender would be byte-swapped, so PT 10 does NOT mean
          interoperable L16. A dynamic PT (96-127) avoids the
          association. Packets with any other PT are rejected with
          a log (S24LE uses its own PT below).

    config MICHI_AUDIO_RTP_PT_S24LE
        int "RTP payload type for PCM S24LE"
        default 96
        range 96 127
        help
          Declared mapping for the S24LE meta: PT 96 is a dynamic type
          (RFC 3551 dynamic range 96-127). Phase 11 does NOT support
          S24LE: such packets are rejected with a log. Range 96-127 so
          the constant can never collide with a static RFC 3551 type.

    config MICHI_AUDIO_JITTER_MAX_MS
        int "Jitter buffer capacity (ms)"
        default 500
        range 50 2000
        help
          Packet-level jitter buffer capacity, expressed in 10 ms
          packets (500 ms = 50 packets). The per-session payload pool is
          capacity x MICHI_AUDIO_RX_BUF_BYTES in PSRAM, so 500 ms/8192 B
          costs ~400 KB. Larger values absorb longer network stalls at
          the cost of PSRAM and startup latency.

    config MICHI_AUDIO_PREFILL_MS
        int "Jitter buffer prefill before playback (ms)"
        default 80
        range 10 1000
        help
          Audio buffered into the jitter buffer before the session
          starts writing to the pipeline (clamped at runtime to
          MICHI_AUDIO_JITTER_MAX_MS). After every underrun a fixed
          re-prefill of 250 ms (MICHI_AUDIO_REPREFILL_MS) is used,
          independent of this value.

    config MICHI_AUDIO_RX_BUF_BYTES
        int "Session UDP receive buffer size (bytes)"
        default 8192
        range 512 65535
        help
          Size of the datagram buffer and of each jitter-buffer payload
          slot. 8192 fits a 10 ms packet at 96 kHz/24-bit stereo
          (5760 B), the largest packet the declared metas produce.
          Datagrams larger than this are truncated by recvfrom.

    config MICHI_AUDIO_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Session task stack size (bytes)"
        default 6144
        range 4096 32768
        help
          Stack of the per-session task (socket I/O, RTP parse, jitter
          buffer insert, blocking pipeline writes). The datagram and
          silence buffers live on the heap, not the stack.

endmenu
